WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.343
Week eight.

00:00:01.393 --> 00:00:06.720
Creating advertising that works, with Andrew Baxter, after twenty six years running agencies.

00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:08.845
Advertising is simple.

00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:09.872
The right message,

00:00:09.922 --> 00:00:10.899
to the right person,

00:00:10.949 --> 00:00:11.870
in the right place,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.317
at the right time.

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:18.981
It runs in four steps: strategy, the idea, making it, and placing it.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:23.379
A billboard gets a two second glance, so use fifteen words or fewer.

00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:26.631
One message per ad, like Kraft's hunger blaster.

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:32.741
The funnel runs from awareness, to knowledge, liking, preference, conviction, and purchase.

00:00:32.791 --> 00:00:36.241
Reach about sixty five percent, at least three times.

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.004
The best ads are famous and emotional.

00:00:39.054 --> 00:00:42.145
John Lewis's Monty the Penguin returned eight to one.

00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:45.451
And differentiation is the most important brand driver,

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:46.444
ahead of relevance,

00:00:46.494 --> 00:00:47.294
esteem and knowledge.

00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:52.437
A successful campaign now averages ten channels, measured by mix modelling.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.963
And about ninety five percent of purchases are intuitive.

00:00:56.013 --> 00:00:58.307
We buy, then post-rationalise.

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:00.601
Create famous work that works.
